{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>וברכך</b> Two times in the Masorah: this one. And the other, regarding the Hebrew servant: \"let it not seem hard in your eyes\" and so forth, \"and YHWH your Elohim will bless you.\" And this is what the Sages said, that the Hebrew servant is not practiced outside the Land — just as here, for it is written \"וברכך in the land\" etc.; there too, specifically in the Land."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "The two occurrences are Deuteronomy 30:16 (here) and Deuteronomy 15:18 (the Hebrew servant passage). The second occurrence actually reads וברכך only in some textual traditions; the standard text of Deut. 15:18 reads וברכך יהוה אלהיך."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:11:07.687520890Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}